<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50826" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīcātim</span></b> , adv.
		vicus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>From street to street</i>, <i>through
				the streets</i>, Sisenn. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p.
				188, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 41 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 95</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod. 5,
				97</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>From village to village</i>, <i>through the villages</i>, <i>in hamlets</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">habitare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					9, 13, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dispersa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 26, 30, § 117</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
